# Every key here is read back from the running tmux, not from tmux/tmux.conf —
# so this pane describes the machine it is on. On this repo's config that means
# the prefix is Ctrl-a, splits are | and -, and the mouse is on; on a stock tmux
# the same rows will say Ctrl-b, % and ".
name:    tmux
what:    keeps things running when the connection drops
check:   tmux
install: sudo dnf install tmux   /   sudo apt install tmux
docs:    man tmux — and tmux/tmux.conf in this repo is short enough to read
probe:   tmux
conf:    ~/.tmux.conf

= SESSIONS — the reason it exists
@detach-client       | detach. Everything inside keeps running, agent included
@choose-tree -Zs     | pick a session from a list, without leaving tmux
@rename-session      | rename the current session

= WINDOWS — like browser tabs
@new-window          | new window
@rename-window       | rename the current window
@next-window         | next window
@previous-window     | previous window
@choose-tree -Zw     | choose from every window in every session
@kill-window         | close the window, after a confirmation

= PANES — two things side by side
@split-window -h     | split left and right, in the same directory
@split-window -v     | split top and bottom
@select-pane -L      | move to the pane on the left
@select-pane -R      | the pane on the right
@select-pane -U      | the pane above
@select-pane -D      | the pane below
@resize-pane -Z      | zoom this pane to fill the window. Again to go back
@kill-pane           | close this pane, after a confirmation
@select-pane -t :.+  | cycle to the next pane
@next-layout         | cycle through the preset layouts
@break-pane          | break this pane out into its own window

= THE MOUSE — on, and the reason day one is survivable
click            | focus a pane
drag a border    | resize
scroll           | scroll back through output
drag to select   | copy, if your terminal emulator supports it

= SCROLLING BACK — 50,000 lines of it
@copy-mode           | enter copy mode, then arrow keys or PgUp to scroll
q                | leave copy mode
@paste-buffer        | paste what you copied
/  (in copy mode)| search backwards through the scrollback

= WHEN SOMETHING IS WRONG
@source-file         | reload the config without restarting
@clock-mode          | a clock, which proves the prefix is reaching tmux
@list-keys           | every binding this tmux knows about
@send-prefix         | send a literal prefix key to the program inside
